  "scope": {
    "description": "Published C behavior consumed by B, cross-release output meaning, and B behavior when C returns no numeric score.",
    "name": "Dify Workflow-as-Tool C to B to A semantic slice"
  },
  "constraints": [
    "Only a Workflow that starts with a User Input node can be turned into a reusable Tool; a Chatflow cannot be used as a Tool.",
    "C, B, and A are independently managed workflows with separate draft and publication lifecycles.",
    "B invokes C as a published Tool by workflow identity, and A publishes what B reports as publishable.",
    "C Version 2 is the latest published version and exposes quality_rating:number; C Version 1 exposes quality_score:number.",
    "quality_score and quality_rating are distinct published output fields; equivalence, rename continuity, and value compatibility must not be asserted.",
    "When C's classifier dependency is unavailable, C can complete successfully without a numeric score and return a diagnostic code.",
    "B's action when C has no numeric score remains explicitly unknown; no block, continue, retry, or review behavior is asserted."
  ],
